# Build outputs, host-platform binaries and local credentials do not belong in a
# build context. `.git` is deliberately NOT listed: the catalog checker asks git
# whether OPEN-ITEMS.md is tracked, and fails the build when it cannot answer.

**/node_modules
frontend/dist
frontend/storybook-static
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
.venv
venv
*.venv
Keys
backend/logs

# The vendored reference — the TrueForge codebase, kept on disk to read and out of the
# history (see .gitignore). The Dockerfile copies the repository with `COPY . .`, so what
# is present locally rides into the image: 105 MB of someone else's code in a production
# container that never reads a byte of it. A build from a clone does not have these; this
# is for the one built on a machine that does.
trueforge
packages
docs
python
RELEASING.md
SECURITY.md
